    "field": "argument_node.kind",
    "value": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.doc",
    "value": "Per-set squared bound. 2 (P(A) − Q(A))² ≤ klDivReal P Q for any measurable set A, given P ≪ Q and finite KL."
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.pretty",
    "value": "∀ {α : Type u_1} [inst : MeasurableSpace α] (P Q : MeasureTheory.Measure α) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P]\n  [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure Q],\n  P.AbsolutelyContinuous Q →\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable (MeasureTheory.llr P Q) P →\n      ∀ (A : Set α), MeasurableSet A → 2 * (P.real A - Q.real A) ^ 2 ≤ InformationTheory.klDivReal P Q"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klDivReal"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.binary_pinsker"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin_le_klDivReal"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klDivReal_nonneg"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.pinsker_proof"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin_le_klDivReal"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.kind",
    "value": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.doc",
    "value": "Data processing inequality for indicators. For probability measures P ≪ Q with finite KL divergence and any measurable set A, the binary KL between the marginals on (A, Aᶜ) is bounded by the full KL: klBin(P(A), Q(A)) ≤ klDivReal P Q."
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.pretty",
    "value": "∀ {α : Type u_1} [inst : MeasurableSpace α] (P Q : MeasureTheory.Measure α) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P]\n  [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure Q],\n  P.AbsolutelyContinuous Q →\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable (MeasureTheory.llr P Q) P →\n      ∀ (A : Set α), MeasurableSet A → InformationTheory.klBin (P.real A) (Q.real A) ≤ InformationTheory.klDivReal P Q"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klDivReal"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin_eq_klFun_sum"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klDivReal_eq_toReal_klDiv"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klFun_integral_ge_of_measurableSet"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.two_sq_sub_le_klDivReal"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klFun_integral_ge_of_measurableSet"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.kind",
    "value": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.doc",
    "value": "Jensen on a subset. For a finite measure Q and a measurable set A with positive mass, if f and klFun ∘ f are integrable and f ≥ 0 almost everywhere, then Q(A) · klFun((1/Q(A)) · ∫_A f dQ) ≤ ∫_A klFun(f) dQ."
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.pretty",
    "value": "∀ {α : Type u_1} [inst : MeasurableSpace α] {Q : MeasureTheory.Measure α} [MeasureTheory.IsFiniteMeasure Q] (f : α → ℝ),\n  MeasureTheory.Integrable f Q →\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => InformationTheory.klFun (f x)) Q →\n      (∀ᵐ (x : α) ∂Q, 0 ≤ f x) →\n        ∀ {A : Set α},\n          0 < Q.real A →\n            Q.real A * InformationTheory.klFun ((Q.real A)⁻¹ * ∫ (x : α) in A, f x ∂Q) ≤\n              ∫ (x : α) in A, InformationTheory.klFun (f x) ∂Q"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin_le_klDivReal"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin_eq_klFun_sum"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.kind",
    "value": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.doc",
    "value": "Algebraic identity. The binary KL factors through klFun: klBin p q = q · klFun(p/q) + (1 − q) · klFun((1 − p)/(1 − q))."
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.pretty",
    "value": "∀ (p q : ℝ),\n  0 < q →\n    q < 1 →\n      InformationTheory.klBin p q =\n        q * InformationTheory.klFun (p / q) + (1 - q) * InformationTheory.klFun ((1 - p) / (1 - q))"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin_le_klDivReal"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.binary_pinsker"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.kind",
    "value": "theorem"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.doc",
    "value": "Binary Pinsker inequality. 2 (p − q)² ≤ klBin p q for p ∈ [0, 1], q ∈ (0, 1). Sharp constant 2."
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.pretty",
    "value": "∀ (p q : ℝ), 0 ≤ p → p ≤ 1 → 0 < q → q < 1 → 2 * (p - q) ^ 2 ≤ InformationTheory.klBin p q"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.antitoneOn_g"
  },
  {
    "field": "argument_node.decl_name",
    "value": "InformationTheory.klBin_one_left"
  },
  {
